      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is no single global legal standard, but major platforms generally rely on context clues like the presence of clear political figures as targets or deepfake heavy manipulations to flag content as hate speech rather than satire. Your internal guidelines should prioritize \"most harmful intent\" and \"real-world harm\" over simple category labels to align with both US law and international human rights principles. It is crucial to document specific \"not acceptable\" examples of satire that cause harm and train your team to make nuanced, case-by-case determinations until your specific policy is legally vetted by counsel.",
