      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The industry is indeed shifting toward a stricter \"harm theory\" standard, where content is removed if it genuinely incites hostility or reinforces harmful stereotypes, regardless of its political context. While satire is still protected if it clearly references a public official or uses recognizable humor, the threshold is lower if the content is deeply misleading or lacks sufficient context to avoid being seen as a threat. You should incorporate this proactive stance into your guidelines to align with high-profile platforms, but ensure your \"harmful content\" definition is carefully nuanced to avoid over-moderation of legitimate political commentary.",
